  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Now, a factory has assembly lines."
   ],
   [
    2.839,
    "In a cell they are called metabolic pathways."
   ],
   [
    5.638,
    "A pathway begins with a specific starting molecule, call it A."
   ],
   [
    9.779,
    "One reaction changes it into B."
   ],
   [
    12.109,
    "Another changes B into C."
   ],
   [
    14.258,
    "And a third makes D, the product."
   ],
   [
    16.654,
    "Each of those steps is catalyzed by an enzyme, and each step has its own."
   ],
   [
    21.432,
    "Enzyme one, enzyme two, enzyme three."
   ],
   [
    25.169,
    "So the answer to what catalyzes each step is a specific enzyme, not one enzyme for the whole line."
   ],
   [
    31.523,
    "Three reactions, three enzymes."
   ],
   [
    34.141,
    "Think of a factory line, where each worker has exactly one job."
   ],
   [
    38.333,
    "We will keep coming back to this strip all chapter."
   ]
  ]
